\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Repeated  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1998\par 16:28\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market repeatedly Monday morning,\par selling U.S. dollars at C$1.5245 and C$1.5250 in an effort\par to contain volatility, said a trader in Toronto.\par    Traders said that after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's initial\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at C$1.5240 failed to halt the U.S. dollar's\par advance, the bank has been selling moderate amounts of U.S.\par dollars at each 5-tick rise by the U.S. unit.\par    The bank's actions have as yet had little effect, as the\par U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5253 as of 10:25 a.m. EDT\par (1425 GMT).\par    The Canadian unit was driven sharply lower in North\par American trading Monday from overnight weakness in the wake\par of Russia's devaluation of the ruble, and a resurgence of\par latent speculative pressure, which had been largely contained\par after the bank adopted more aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tactics\par in support of the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over a week ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The Canadian dollar has been under severe downward\par pressure in recent months, prompting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's more\par aggressive, activist tactics.\par    Analysts say the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has fundamental\par weaknesses stemming from low commodity prices and global\par uncertainties stemming from the renewed economic and\par financial turmoil in Asia and Russia.\par    The intense pressure on the Canadian dollar is expected\par to last until the pressures originating in Asia relent, or\par the Bank of Canada raises interest rates to defend the\par embattled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-17-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1028EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8h01yks\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
