\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank of Canada -2: Estimates Of Amount Spent Vary \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1998\par 22:03\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The bank's recent shift to early \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is far from unprecedented, C.T. Securities' Pyle said. \par \par \uc2  The bank was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  before 70-tick moves in January, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also under acute pressure, he pointed out. \par \par \uc2  Bank officials have not abandoned their usual pattern of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 70-tick moves despite the fact that they are coming in early then they judge it appropriate, Pyle said. \par \par \uc2  "If the bank feels that it is in a different type of climate where there is a lot of pressure - or undue pressure - on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , then it is going to leave that rule on the shelf," he said. \par \par \uc2  The market will continue to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve, Pyle said. \par \par \uc2  The key question now is whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has established a level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. Some market watchers believe that it has targeted a Canadian dollar worth 65 cents U.S. (or a U.S. dollar level of C$1.5385) as the level it will defend. \par \par \uc2  Unlike some observers, who laud the bank's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactics and believe it may have staved off an interest rate increase in defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Pyle offers a more restrained assessment of the bank's approach. \par \par \uc2  "I think it was necessary for the bank to try to convince the market that there was independent policy at hand, that this simply wasn't a 'let it drift' policy co-ordinated by the Bank of Canada and the federal government," he said. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been better served by a sudden, surprise rate hike, Pyle argued. \par \par \uc2  He estimates that the bank may have spent about 10% of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves - reported at US$22.5 billion in July - during the last week or so. \par \par \uc2  "It wasn't cheap \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , by any stretch of the imagination," Pyle said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  only releases details of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spending on a monthly basis. The August release is scheduled for Sept. 3. \par \par \uc2  Estimates of the amount spent since the bank began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively on Aug. 7 have varied considerably, ranging from around US$1 billion to US$2 billion or more. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  08-17-98 \par \par \uc2  1603EDT \par \par \uc2  4219 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8h01ywt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
