\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian dollar opens firmer, helped by Asia gains. \b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 15:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.5125/1.5230\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.5170\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.5119 RESISTANCE 1.5269  HIGH 1.5188 LOW 1.5157 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.5178 HIGH 1.5188\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.5156\par PREV CLOSE  1.5194 LOW  1.5157\tab HIGH 1.5175 LOW 1.5155\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THURSDAY, AUGUST 14\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL, ACTIVITY: MODERATE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Canada's dollar opened firmer at C$1.5178 (US$0.6588) in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moderately active trading on Friday. * Dealers said the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  benefited from gains in Hong Kong's stock market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overnight and some strength in the Japanese yen. * Repeated\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during the past week is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to limit any declines by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, Aug 14 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar opened firmer in moderate trading on Friday, benefiting from overnight gains in Hong Kong's stock market and some strength in the Japanese yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian dollar firmed to open at C$1.5178 (US$0.6588), up from C$1.5194 (US$0.6582) at Thursday's close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The yen's a little bit better, and Canada's tracked the yen," said Reid Farrill, executive director, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at CIBC Wood Gundy Securities Inc.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's a combination of a stronger yen and the Bank (of Canada) helping things along the way," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets for the fifth consecutive trading day. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has moved from a policy of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to smooth out gyrations in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to aggressively defending the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to buy Canadian dollars for U.S. dollars at around C$1.5200 (US$0.6579). That figure is seen by some market players as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's near-term ceiling for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, the Canadian dollar firmed to 1.1806 marks from 1.1739 marks, and firmed to 95.66 marks from 95.35 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In economic news, the Canadian composite leading indicator rose 0.3 percent in July to 207.7 (base 1981) after an 0.5 percent rise in June, Statistics Canada said on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The indicator foreshadows economic activity by tabulating figures for sectors that rise or fall in advance of broader movements in the economy. The figure is "smoothed", reflecting a moving average of approximately the past five months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Reuters survey of economists had forecast on average the smoothed index would show a rise 0.4 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Jeffrey Hodgson, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8105, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8e036a4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
