\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian dollar closes stronger in light trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 500 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 22:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.5125/1.5230\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.5170\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.5119 RESISTANCE 1.5269  HIGH 1.5188 LOW 1.5157 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.5178 HIGH 1.5192\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.5156\par PREV CLOSE  1.5194 LOW  1.5155\tab HIGH 1.5175 LOW 1.5155\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday, AUGUST 14\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL, ACTIVITY: LIGHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Canada's dollar closed stronger at C$1.5171 (US$0.6592) in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par session of quiet trading on Friday. * Dealers said some small\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying against the mark and yen benefited the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . * Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Canada was absent from the market for the first time in six\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading sessions. * Dealers said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's previous\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has set a near-term ceiling on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market anxiously awaiting next week's developments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, Aug 14 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar closed stronger in a session of quiet, rangebound trading on Friday, helped by modest buying against the German mark and Japanese yen, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian dollar ended the session at C$1.5171 (US$0.6592), firmer from C$1.5194 (US$0.6582) at Thursday's close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There was very, very light activity. Really the market is nervous ahead of Clinton (testimony) on Monday, and Russia's having a bit of impact on the mark," said one trader with a Canadian bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think there's been some Canada/mark buying that's been behind the scenes, and maybe a little bit of Canada/yen buying, but nothing large enough to really move the market," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of Canada was absent from the market for the first time in six consecutive trading sessions. But dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's previous aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had set a temporary ceiling on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which few speculators were willing to challenge.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has moved from a policy of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to smooth out gyrations in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to aggressively defending the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Maybe they would have been in at C$1.5195, maybe they would have been in at the figure (C$1.5200) again. We never really got it up to test it," said another Toronto-based trader.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the market is nervously eyeing a number of developments next week, including the situation in Russia where financial markets there tumbled on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The scary thing about this whole thing is if Russia does blow up, and if they have to raise money because they can't get it from the IMF, they're going to have to sell some commodities, which in turn will hurt us," said the first trader.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The strength of the Canadian dollar is still tied closely to commodity prices because the country's economy remains largely resource-based.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, the Canadian dollar firmed to 1.1870 marks from 1.1739 marks, and rose to 96.39 marks from 95.35 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Jeffrey Hodgson, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8105, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8e035j1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
