\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Afternoon: C$ Up Slightly, BOC Doesn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1998\par 21:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar ended slightly higher after a day of quiet trading Friday, the first day since last Thursday when the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on its behalf. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5170 at 3:56 p.m. EDT (1956 GMT), down slightly from C$1.5172 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) and from C$1.5190 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "I think people were a little bit on guard, waiting for something more to happen," said one Toronto \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. "All week, players have been taking their sticks and poking the Bank of Canada to see where it's going to show up," he added. \par \par \uc2  The trader said trading in the Canadian unit followed the same pattern as has recurred all week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened in the morning, and then weakened in the afternoon as traders started probing for a response from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which adopted a new policy of unpredictable \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last week. \par \par \uc2  "We traded a bit off the back of (U.S.) dollar/yen, too," he said. "We (U.S.) dollar/yen went bid, so did (U.S.) dollar/Canada." That pushed the U.S. to its high around C$1.5185, the trader said. \par \par \uc2  "From there, I think it was just a matter of it running out of gas. People had a long enough week at it, and just squared up any long U.S. dollar positions," he said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was moderate to light, the trader noted. \par \par \uc2  Katherine Beattie, a technical analyst with Standard & Poor's MMS, said this week's relatively flat performance by the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  presaged a similar pattern next week. \par \par \uc2  "We're looking for activity to remain quiet," she said. "While we're not looking for it to sell off next week, I don't see it improving either." \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar will likely replicate this week's trading range of C$1.5115 to C$1.5255, she said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 3:56 p.m. EDT (1956 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Thursday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.5170      1.5172   1.5190\par    CDN/DEM     1.1872      1.1780   1.1738\par    CDN/YEN     96.43       95.62    96.36\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1958GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8e06xb8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
