\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar opens firmer as dollar/yen dips. \b0\par\par\uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1998\par 15:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.5130/1.5230\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.5215\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.5050 RESISTANCE 1.5355  HIGH 1.5221 LOW 1.5154 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.5175 HIGH 1.5175\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.5186\par PREV CLOSE  1.5193 LOW  1.5154\tab HIGH 1.5201 LOW 1.5155\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THURSDAY, AUGUST 13\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL, ACTIVITY: ACTIVE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada's dollar opened firmer at C$1.5175 (US$0.6590) as U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar again slipped against yen on Bank of Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fears. *\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was maintaining overnight gains after opening.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Market watching for Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy up\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after such action for four consecutive trading days.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *U.S. July retail sales down 0.4 percent, first drop since 0.2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent decline in October 1997, *Ex-auto retail sales up 0.5\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent, auto sales drop of 3.0 percent steepest since 3.3\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent drop in April 1997. *U.S. jobless claims fell to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 301,000 in Aug 8 week from revised 308,000 in previous week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada's June car sales down 3.1 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, Aug 13 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar opened a bit firmer at C$1.5175 (US$0.6590) on Thursday as the U.S. dollar dipped to around 145 yen again on fears of Bank of Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market is watching for the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to step into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and buy up Canada to limit any rally in the U.S. dollar following four straight trading days of buy-Canada \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was on the defensive on Wednesday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  all afternoon from C$1.5168 (US$0.6593) up to C$1.5220 (US$0.6570). Traders are watching to see if the bank can defend the key level of C$1.5230 (US$0.6566), where it stepped in on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The recovery looks fragile because it stems largely from the yen's rise against the U.S. dollar, which tends to spill over into dollar/Canada trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Concern over Russia's financial system, however, is propping up the U.S. dollar on expectations of flight to quality capital flows into U.S. dollar assets from affected regions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, the Canadian unit rose to 1.1792 marks after 1.1747 marks at the previous close here, but fell to 95.76 yen after 96.08 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the fundamental side, the U.S. economy showed strong growth in consumer spending in data released this morning.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. July retail sales fell 0.4 percent, the first drop since a 0.2-percent decline in October 1997. But excluding the impact of the General Motors strike, the ex-auto retail sales rose 0.5 percent. A 3.0-percent drop in automobile sales was the steepest since a 3.3-percent drop in April 1997.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. jobless claims fell to 301,000 in the August 8 week from a revised 308,000 in the previous week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada's June car sales were down 3.1 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economists on average had forecast a drop of 2.4 percent in Canada's new motor vehicle sales. Statistics Canada said June's decline was the first month-over-month decline since January 1998 and the second largest decline since May 1997.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the bigger picture of the economy, the second-quarter gross domestic product and current account data will be released on August 31. Canada will release its July merchandise trade data on August 18.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian dollar was trading slightly firmer in early trading after the opening, thanks to a rise in the yen against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Because dollar/yen is lower, dollar/Canada is trading down to C$1.5140 (US$0.6605)," one trader said. "It kind of feels that the dollar/yen looks falling through 144.80 yen, then dollar/Canada falls through the C$1.5140 level."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the market was still disappointed over Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday, which failed to stop the U.S. dollar's rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8d032rf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
