\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Afternoon: C$ Steady After 6th Straight  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1998\par 22:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar ended nearly even with Wednesday's official closing level against the U.S. dollar, in the sixth consecutive session in which the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5190 at 4:20 p.m. EDT (2020 GMT), up from C$1.5175 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) but down slightly from C$1.5204 late Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official Wednesday close for the U.S. dollar was C$1.5193. \par \par \uc2  Traders described a rather lackluster session of trading Thursday, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  mounting two light afternoon rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the Canadian dollar after it began edging up against the psychologically important C$1.5200 mark. \par \par \uc2  In the morning session, some said the Canadian dollar had a good bid on rumors that a major foreign investment house had issued a buy Canada recommendation, but the bid dwindled when the rumors could not be confirmed, and on a firming of the U.S. dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  While many feel the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are gradually losing their sting, some also said the bank's apparently modest goal of simply limiting further Canadian-dollar depreciation is having its intended effects. \par \par \uc2  "There's more accounts out there that seem to be tired of being long in U.S. dollars," said Bill Mooney, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Societe Generale in Montreal. "They're just not getting the run-up to C$1.5250 that they thought they'd get." \par \par \uc2  Mooney said that there is some latent buy-Canada sentiment in the market, but persistent fears of instability from Russia and Japan are keeping it in the closet. He said that for the time being, continued \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to keep the U.S. dollar/\b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rate confined to a relatively narrow range below C$1.5200. \par \par \uc2  "The market knows the bank is out there, and it's no longer taking a wild run at the Canadian dollar," he added. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 4:20 p.m. EDT (2020 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Wednesday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.5190      1.5175   1.5204\par    CDN/DEM     1.1738      1.1775   1.1744\par    CDN/YEN     95.36       95.91    96.16\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2025GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8d06wb2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
