\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Bank Seen Willing To Spend \b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1998\par 20:32\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Thursday, selling U.S. dollars\par at C$1.5200, said a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader in Toronto.\par    The U.S. dollar leveled off after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par was hovering at C$1.5194 at 2:22 a.m. EDT (1822 GMT).\par    It had been edging higher against the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par through the late morning and early afternoon.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  followed the pattern of early\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  established last Friday and then repeated every\par day this week.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's previous, unofficial policy was to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets after intraday moves in either\par direction of 70 ticks or more in order to contain\par volatility. The U.S. dollar closed at C$1.5193 Wednesday,\par meaning that the bank was once again entering markets much\par earlier than its previous policy would dictate.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared willing to commit more funds\par to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  than it has in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par actions earlier this week, the trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    While Friday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was described as massive by\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market sources - reportedly involving as much as\par US$1 billion or more - the size of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par believed to have dwindled this week.\par    Analysts blame the weakness in the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par the low commodity prices and global uncertainties stemming\par from the renewed economic and financial turmoil in Asia and\par Russia.\par    Market watchers said the bank's new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy\par was an attempt to re-establish a "two-way risk" in the\par market for the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been on almost continuous,\par uninterrupted slide since it broke through its all-time low\par in early June and then kept pushing through into previously\par uncharted territory,.\par    The intense pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to last\par until the pressures originating in Asia relent, or the Bank\par of Canada raises interest rates to defend the embattled\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Some market watchers have said sustained negative yield\par spreads between Canada and the U.S. are also a key reason\par for the Canadian dollar's weakness, but Canadian bond yields\par have crept above U.S. yields in recent sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-13-98\par \f2