\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  dollar ends up but off  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  highs. \b0\par\par\uc2 878 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 23:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.5110/1.5230\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.5215\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.5050 RESISTANCE 1.5355  HIGH 1.5238 LOW 1.5118 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.5133 HIGH 1.5205\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.5204\par PREV CLOSE  1.5224 LOW  1.5115\tab HIGH 1.5230 LOW 1.5120\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WEDNESDAY, AUGUST 12\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL, ACTIVITY: ACTIVE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada's dollar ended firmer at C$1.5193 (US$0.6582), but lost earlier gains\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from yen's overnight rise and Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . *The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bought \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at C$1.5168 (US$0.6593) in late morning. *Focus on renewed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par safe-haven buying of U.S. dollar assets as market concerned about Russia's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par financial crisis and despite fears of Bank of Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/yen. *BOC stressed in its quarterly review that underlying momentum in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic economy positive, although that GM and other strikes lowered its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par estimate for Q2 GDP growth to annual rate of 2.5 percent from 3.0 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, Aug 12 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar ended Wednesday's session slightly firmer at C$1.5193 (US$0.6582), giving up most of its earlier gains on yen's overnight rise and persistent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for four business days in a row.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to drift lower after official trading hours here, although it has scored two wins against one loss at the close level versus the U.S. dollar this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Unlike the last two days of buy-Canada \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , today's action lacked a sharp edge\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's been a passive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," one trader said. "The market hasn't lost confidence in the bank, it just doesn't scare them (traders) any more."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He puts today's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at US$450 million, bigger than US$5 million each on Tuesday and Monday, but smaller than last Friday's, estimated to total more than US$500 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It was a very negative signal that they put in the market," another trader said. "Their lack of aggressiveness is going to hurt them significantly. It's going to be a turning point, especially if it goes back to C$1.5230/35 (US$0.6566/0.6564), the level of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In late morning on Wednesday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared to have taken some in the market off guard by waiting until long U.S. dollar positions built up before stepping in to sell U.S. dollars, at C$1.5168 (US$0.6593).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the bank was on the defensive in the afternoon, trying to smooth out a rise the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Growing concern over Russia's financial system boosted the U.S. dollar against key \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , particularly the mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It was reflected in cross trading. The Canadian unit extended gains to 1.1747 marks after 1.1695 marks at the previous close here, but fell to 96.08 yen after 96.70 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier Canada started the day firmer at C$1.5133 (US$0.6608), piggybacking on a sharp overnight rise in the yen against the U.S. dollar on growing fears that the Bank of Japan would not tolerate a further decline in the yen's value.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the whole, Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has shifted its tactics by making pre-emptive attacks on speculators testing the downside of the local dollar, starting with massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bank, seeking to establish two-way risks in U.S. dollar/Canada trade, was previously seen stepping into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on Tuesday morning to cap the U.S. dollar's gain at C$1.5230 (US$0.6566).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of Canada remained positive about the outlook for the domestic economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It said in a quarterly review on Wednesday that the underlying momentum in the economy was positive, although it had lowered its estimate for the gross domestic growth (GDP) for the second quarter to an annual rate of 2.5 percent from an earlier projection of 3.0 percent in the wake of General Motors and construction sector strikes.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The second-quarter GDP and current account data will be released on August 31. Canada will release its July merchandise trade data on August 18.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of Canada does not think investors have lost confidence in holding Canadian securities yet.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Overall the weakness in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is overdone," said Rob Palombi, senior fixed-income analyst at Standard & Poor's MMS. "Once we take the Asian uncertainty out of the equation, we could see a fairly significant rebound in the Canadian dollar."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "When that will happen is still very unclear, but against that background, a large risk premium built into the 10-year and 30-year area (in the bond market) over the past couple of weeks, I would imagine, is attracting buyers, especially when supply is declining more rapidly for longer-term issues," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin and Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa will meet in San Francisco early next month to discuss a wide range of issues, including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves, after Miyazawa took office earlier this month under the government.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8c02zju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
