\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Canada buys Canadian dlrs at C$1.5168. \b0\par\par\uc2 161 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 17:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, Aug 12 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday morning \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fourth consecutive trading day to buy up Canadian dollars for U.S. dollars, this time at C$1.5168 (US$0.6593), traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shifted its tactics by making pre-emptive attacks on speculators testing the downside of the local dollar, starting with massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Friday. \par \par \uc2  The bank, seeking to establish two-way risks in U.S. dollar/Canada trade, was previously seen stepping into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday morning to cap the U.S. dollar's gain at C$1.5230 (US$0.6566). \par \par \uc2  Earlier this morning, the Canadian dollar opened 100 points firmer at C$1.5133 (US$0.6608), piggybacking on a sharp overnight rise in the yen against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  ((Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8c02zef\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
