\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Once Again  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Early \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 17:51\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market late Thursday morning to sell U.S. dollars at C$1.5168, said a trader in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  Other sources also reported the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling U.S. dollars around C$1.5160. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar leveled off after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was hovering at C$1.5142 at 11:41 a.m. EDT (1541 GMT). \par \par \uc2  It dipped as low as C$1.5117 at 8:02 a.m. EDT (1202 GMT), but was hovering in a broad range around C$1.5140 for most of the morning before heading higher just prior to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It closed at C$1.5224 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came just as information about the Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quarterly review was released. \par \par \uc2  In the report, bank officials suggested Canadian growth in the second quarter was around 2.5% at annualized rates. They had earlier been predicted that growth would be at about 3.5% to the middle of 1999. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  follows the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent pattern of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets much earlier than its previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy would dictate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's previous unofficial policy was to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after intraday moves in either direction of 70 ticks or more in order to contain volatility, but beginning last Friday, the bank began a pattern of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market early and at unpredictable levels. \par \par \uc2  Friday's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been followed by smaller \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  every morning this week. \par \par \uc2  The bank's new approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is designed to create a "two-way flow" in the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been under severe downward pressure in recent weeks, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  Analysts blame the negative sentiment on the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the low commodity prices and global uncertainties stemming from the renewed economic and financial turmoil in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Some market watchers also attributed part of the pressure to negative yield spreads between Canada and the U.S., but Canadian yields have moved over U.S. yields across most of the curve in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-12-98 \par \par \uc2  1151EDT \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8c01vs8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
