\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Latin American  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Dn On Russia \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 22:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  As well, the Russian parliament decided Wednesday not to convene a special session next week to discuss austerity bills that represent the centerpiece of the government's efforts to shore up its ailing markets and restore confidence in the ruble. \par \par \uc2  The ruble weakened outside its daily declared trading band for the second day in a row and closed lower Wednesday. The dollar for next-day delivery closed at RUR6.3150, up from RUR6.3100 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  The latest developments out of Russia may raise concerns Thursday for emerging markets in general. "I wouldn't be surprised if we seen jitters in Asia tonight," said Eric Nickerson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Bank of America in New York. \par \par \uc2  Already Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  registered sharp losses late Wednesday as the Mexican peso, the Brazilian real and Venezuelan bolivar closed lower. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City on the 48-hour spot dollar markets, banking leader Banamex quoted the U.S. dollar closing at a mid-rate of MXN9.2550, higher from MXN9.1920 on Tuesday's close. The dollar rose to BRL1.1722 against the real, from from Tuesday's close of BRL1.1686. \par \par \uc2  The Chilean peso ended higher against the U.S. dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keeping a tight lid on liquidity to stem the dollar's rise against the peso, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In commodity-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Australian dollar and the Canadian dollar strengthened on the yen's recovery Wednesday. Even so, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice Wednesday at the level of CS$1.5168, which indicated to traders that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would like to see a stronger Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 12-08-98 \par \par \uc2  2028GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 20714 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8c06sw8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
