\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar steady,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  sells U.S. dlrs. \b0\par\par\uc2 720 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 16:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.5160/1.5250\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.5205\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.5100 RESISTANCE 1.5350  HIGH 1.5216 LOW 1.5176 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.5213 HIGH 1.5228\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.5204\par PREV CLOSE  1.5178 LOW  1.5176\tab HIGH 1.5215 LOW 1.5175\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TUESDAY, AUGUST 11\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL, ACTIVITY: MODERATE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada's dollar was trading steady around C$1.5200 (US$0.6579)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in early trade following \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollars at C$1.5230 (US$0.6566). *Canada opened a bit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weaker at C$1.5213 (US$0.6573). *BOC continued to step in for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par third straight trading day, after Friday's massive\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . *U.S. dollar rose overnight above 147 yen,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par eight-year high, as Tokyo stocks fell and technical buying\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par emerged. *Market concerned over pace of Japan banking/tax\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reform. *Canada July housing starts fell 6.5 percent, partly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hit by construction strikes in Southern Ontario.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, Aug 11 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar was trading around C$1.5200 (US$0.6579) in early morning on Tuesday, a bit weaker than Monday's level but stable following recent persistent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in early trading to sell U.S. dollars at C$1.5230 (US$0.6566), taking pre-emptive action for the third straight business day before the U.S. dollar rose too fast.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The change in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tactics, begun on Friday with surprise massive U.S. dollar selling, has so far helped stem a further slide in the Canadian dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Yet the outlook for the local dollar is uncertain.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar rose above 147 yen, an eight-year high, overnight on growing concern over Japan's bid to rescue its recession-hit economy through banking and tax reform.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In addition, confidence in Canadian securities as a whole could come under scrutiny again by international investors if the local stock market continued to plunge for a sustained period.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market bears took down Toronto equities with the key index opening down by 59.70 and continued to fall this morning.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The local dollar opened a bit weaker at C$1.5213 (US$0.6573) to the U.S. dollar on Tuesday after closing at C$1.5178 (US$0.6588) here on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    In cross trading, the Canadian unit was little changed at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.1703 marks after 1.1705 marks at the previous close here, and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rose to 96.70 yen after 96.31 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The U.S. dollar was steady as safe-haven buying continued\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over uncertainty in Asia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Tokyo stock prices were depressed as the Japanese economy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stayed stagnant.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indonesia's government said on Tuesday it had deferred some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par principal payments on its foreign debt in August, but that it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was not a default. Paris Club creditor nations said Indonesia\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had been expected to suspend some repayments this month before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they work out debt rescheduling terms in September.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One factor helping stabilise the Canadian dollar is the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par release last Friday of Canada's July jobs data, which showed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher-than-expected growth. Canada's dollar has come under\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure from soft commodity prices sparked by the Asian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par crisis, and more recently, worries over a slower pace of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic economic growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This morning, Canada released July housing starts, which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fell 6.5 percent to a seasonally adjusted annual rate of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 123,100 units from a revised 131,700 in June, partly hit by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par construction strikes in Southern Ontario.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The data tend to fluctuate sharply month by month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The next indicator of overall strength in the Canadian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy is second quarter gross domestic product (GDP) and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par current account data, to be released on August 31.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The GDP report at the end of this month should help\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par refocus the market," said Rob Palombi, senior fixed-income\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analyst at Standard & Poor's MMS. "Growth is slowing down but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par we don't think it's dramatic. In current account we could see a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deterioration, but overall people are still looking at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par current account deficit to GDP ratio of two percent, that's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par actually supportive for the Canadian dollar."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8b02vj6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
