\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Afternoon: C$ Down; Thin Range Trade After BOC Move \b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 22:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar ended down slightly against the U.S. dollar in sluggish trading Tuesday, as another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  was enough to anchor the Canadian unit in a firm range, but not enough to spark a rally. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5220 at 4:08 p.m. EDT (2008 GMT), from C$1.5208 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) and from C$1.5175 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the Canadian dollar for the fourth consecutive session early Tuesday, reportedly selling U.S. dollars at the C$1.5230 U.S. dollar level. As in the previous three sessions, the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came well in advance of its normal 70-tick \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  trigger. \par \par \uc2  With \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now seemingly a regular occurance, traders said speculative U.S. dollar bids have dwindled drastically, since the levels at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step in are as yet unpredictable, although both \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday and Tuesday took place beginning at C$1.5230. \par \par \uc2  "The whole idea of surprise levels is working well because no one's sure when they'll step in - sitting on offers or actively giving bids," said Linda Park, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the Bank of Montreal. "That whole uncertainty is what's created some stability in the market." \par \par \uc2  Some traders said trading Tuesday was confined to a tight range between C$1.5200 and C$1.5220 because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumored to be ready to step in with more U.S. dollar selling if the rate moved much above C$1.5220, while C$1.5230 was considered a sure \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  trigger. \par \par \uc2  Trading was relatively light throughout the day, with the spectre of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and also the turmoil in North American stock markets keeping many to the sidelines. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 4:08 p.m. EDT (2008 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Monday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.5220      1.5208   1.5175\par    CDN/DEM     1.1689      1.1173   1.1713\par    CDN/YEN     96.71       96.31    96.34\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2011GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8b06sbj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
