\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Morning: C$ Dn, But Off Lows, After BOC  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 15:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar is down Tuesday morning but is off its earlier lows after yet another early \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In what has rapidly become a daily pattern, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market to sell U.S. dollars this morning before its usual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggers. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5205 at 9:51 a.m. EDT (1351 GMT), from C$1.5208 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) and from C$1.5175 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The bank started selling U.S. dollars at C$1.5230 shortly after 9 a.m. EDT (1300 GMT). The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  started to slump lower at that point after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's usual \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  window slid shut without any evidence of a rate increase. \par \par \uc2  While some market watchers believe the concerted and repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  the bank started Friday effectively preclude a rate hike - at least in the short term - others believe that an interest rate increase is still extremely likely. \par \par \uc2  The bank's action on Tuesday, although less sweeping and dramatic than Friday's assault on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, has contributed to a certain edginess among Canadian dollar players, said one New York \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  "The market's a little nervous to take the bank on," the trader said. "They've come in a little bit earlier than expected again, and it's been persistent." \par \par \uc2  "There's still underlying demand for U.S. dollars, but it think that will be on the sidelines until the smoke clears a little bit." \par \par \uc2  Trading was active in the period before and during the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action, but has since subsided, the trader said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 9:51 a.m. EDT (1351 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Monday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.5205      1.5208   1.5175\par    CDN/DEM     1.1710      1.1173   1.1713\par    CDN/YEN     96.75       96.31    96.34\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1353GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8b06rgi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
