\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2 -2: Action Early In Session Again \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 15:25\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday to sell U.S. dollars around C$1.5230 in an action similar to Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said a trader in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar dipped immediately after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was hovering at C$1.5207 at 9:17 a.m. EDT (1317 GMT). \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has deviated from its normal, unofficial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in the last three sessions, coming in early and more frequently than usual. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's usual policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after intraday moves in either direction of 70 ticks or more in order to contain volatility. The U.S. dollar closed at C$1.5178 on Monday, meaning that Tuesday's action was somewhat ahead of the normal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  trigger. \par \par \uc2  Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said Tuesday's action was relatively light. Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also widely described as light, while Friday's was said to involve as much as US$ 1 billion. Exact amounts are unknown, since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not release information on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market actions. \par \par \uc2  Some market watchers reported that the bank's offers were not met with the same strong response as on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar has been under severe downward pressure in recent weeks, and was repeatedly puncturing all-time low levels before the bank began its strategy of frequent, irregular \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts blame the recent spate of weakness in the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the low commodity prices and global uncertainties stemming from the renewed economic and financial turmoil in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Some market watchers say negative yield spreads between Canada and the U.S. have also been a key reason for the Canadian dollar's weakness, with a recent string of soft Canadian economic indicators adding to the pressure. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-11-98 \par \par \uc2  0925EDT \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8b01u0a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
