\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Alone Seen Insufficient \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 20:32\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  With destabilized financial markets potentially threatening economic growth, the bank was compelled to move, Scotiabank's Gampel suggested. \par \par \uc2  "I think that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had decided a degree of urgency had entered into the need to introduce a two-way risk into the marketplace," he said. \par \par \uc2  While the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been effective, at least on a short-term basis, it's done nothing to change the underlying direction for the Canadian dollar, Gampel argued. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is really a sign of weakness rather than strength," he said, adding that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have sufficient \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  indefinitely. \par \par \uc2  Last Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported that it had total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of US$22.52 billion on July 31. \par \par \uc2  And the effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is inherently limited because it ultimately does not address the global economic factors that are undermining the Canadian dollar, he said. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself will likely not have the desired effect...mainly because the Asian situation is not going away," Gampel said. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar stood firm after Tuesday morning's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the U.S. dollar, which was around C$1.5230 when the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hovered at C$1.5207 at 2:12 p.m. EDT (1812 GMT). \par \par \uc2  Rob Palombi, financial markets analyst with Standard & Poor's MMS, believes conditions remain stable enough that the Bank of Canada will hold off on raising rates unless compelled to. \par \par \uc2  "As far as a rate hike goes, nothing has really changed, but if they are absolutely forced into it they will have to raise rates," he said. \par \par \uc2  Palombi sees creating uncertainty as a primary objective of the banks' recent incursions into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think they're trying to draw a line in the sand anywhere," Palombi said. "I don't think this is about monetary conditions. This is just about a more stable range for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and they're doing it by generating some uncertainty." \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  08-11-98 \par \par \uc2  1432EDT \par \par \uc2  4229 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8b01ulg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
