\par\par \b \uc2  Canada bonds end weaker, 30-year spread positive. \b0\par\par\uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1998\par 01:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, Aug 10 (Reuters) - Canadian bonds ended mostly weaker on Monday with the long end of the yield curve falling sharply and the yield on the 30-year bond now offering a higher rate than the U.S. bond for the first time since July 1997. \par \par \uc2  Canada's bonds failed to attract investors as U.S. dollar assets are the investment of choice at a time of global uncertainty and bearish domestic stock performance. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody believes that the Bank of Canada is going to raise interest rates (to protect the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), so the sell-off in the front end has been very marginal," said Rob Palombi, senior fixed-income analyst at Standard & Poor's MMS. \par \par \uc2  Most sectors in Canadian bonds are now offering higher yields than U.S. bonds, reflecting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar has finally stabilised after Friday's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a less aggressive buy-\b \highlight22\uc2 Canada operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, and has ended firmer against the U.S. dollar for two trading days in a row. \par \par \uc2  "The market is basically building in the uncertainty risk premium for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We've been underperforming the U.S. for two and half weeks now," Palombi said. "The 10-year and 30-year have built in a roughly 20-basis point premium." \par \par \uc2  Canada's benchmark 30-year bond (due June 1, 2027) fell C$0.94 at C$132.93 to yield 5.666 percent. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. 30-year bond cut losses, rising 3/32 to yield 5.62 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Canada-U.S. spread in 30-years turned into positive 4.6 basis points from negative 1.6 points at the previous close here. \par \par \uc2  The Canada-U.S. spread could return to parity from positive if the Canadian government's 10-year bond auction later this week produces good results, Palombi said. \par \par \uc2  "The game is over as far as Canadian yields are trading below those in the U.S.," said Jim Webber, director of fixed-income research at TD Securities Inc. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can influence certain rates, but it can't direct the whole market." \par \par \uc2  The bond market has been affected by the weakness in the Canadian dollar in recent trade. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still waiting for some kind of signal on what the bank really wants here," he said. "Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least got a lot of people off guard and was very well done. Whether it's enough to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable beyond the few days, I'm quite doubtful." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada has refrained from raising its key short-term lending rate as a means of boosting the local dollar. Higher borrowing costs for firms and consumers could hurt consumer and business confidence, and it would take more than a rate hike to turn around the current downtrend. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's prime policy is to control inflation, which is still under control. The depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tends to push up import costs, but it has not had a major impact on the inflation front. \par \par \uc2  The money market was firmer in line with the appreciation of the local dollar. \par \par \uc2  Canada's three-month when issued T-bill yielded 5.02 percent after 5.10 percent at the previous close here. \par \par \uc2  ((Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107, \par \par \uc2  toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8a02uxa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
