\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar opens little changed, eye on yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 508 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 15:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.5160/1.5270\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.5215\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.5100  RESISTANCE 1.5350 HIGH 1.5251 LOW 1.5193 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.5233 HIGH 1.5251\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.5222\par PREV CLOSE  1.5218 LOW  1.5193\tab HIGH 1.5240 LOW 1.5190\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MONDAY, AUGUST 10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL, ACTIVITY: MODERATE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada's dollar opened little changed at C$1.5233 (US$0.6565),\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remaining steady on back of Friday's massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Fate of CAD still uncertain as U.S. dollar firming vs yen on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par concern over Japan's banking/tax reform. *Trading cautious,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par focus also on how or whether Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stabilise market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, Aug 10 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar opened little changed at C$1.5233 (US$0.6565) on Monday, after steadying on the back of massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading turned quiet after choppy activity earlier in the morning. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seems stuck in a tight range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "American banks have some interest to sell quite a few (U.S.) dollars and then you've got a typical after-the-Bank-of-Canada-window (for money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), we took the backup towards C$1.5240/45 (US$0.6562/0.6560) level," one Canadian trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "A little bit disappointing after Friday. I didn't expect the bank to raise rates, but I thought if we rallied to C$1.5250 (US$0.6557), the Bank of Canada would come in a similar fashion to Friday," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was no sign of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell U.S. dollars for Canadian on Monday. The bank sold a large amount of U.S. dollars on Friday at various levels, pushing the Canadian dollar up by nearly 250 points. About half of that gain was lost by the end of Friday's session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One factor helping stabilise the local dollar is the release on Friday of Canada's July jobs data, which showed higher-than-expected growth. Canada's dollar has come under pressure from soft commodity prices resulting from the Asian crisis, and more recently from worries about a slower pace of domestic economic growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    In cross trading, the Canadian unit slipped to 1.1684 marks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from 1.1696 marks at the previous close here, and flat at 96.08\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen after 96.07 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakness against the U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could spill over into dollar/Canada trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market is once again disappointed with the slow\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par progress in Tokyo's banking system reforms.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Flight to quality capital is seen flowing into U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par assets as the market is also nervous about the possibility of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par devaluation of China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yuan. Such a measure to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par boost China's exports could trigger similar actions by other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian nations and prompt withdrawal of short-term capital from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the region.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8a02uga\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
