\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Afternoon -2: More  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Seen As Dubious Ploy \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 22:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Still, most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers note that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new proactive defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been sufficient to turn sentiment for the embattled Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around, though it has made it more difficult to take out the kind of short-term speculative positions that were common for the last several weeks. \par \par \uc2  Mooney and others say the market is still rife with speculation about the bank eventually backing its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactics by raising domestic interest rates, although that is seen as less likely this week because of a large bank auction of 10-year government bonds on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Some said a strategy of constant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  without a subsequent rate increase may eventually work against the bank if Canadian dollar bears continually force it to dip into its reserves to play the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  card. \par \par \uc2  "When you've already spent that much money you better be consistent and show up at every corner," said a trader at a Canadian bank. "They had to do it (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) today, and they'll have to do it tomorrow unless a much more decisive action on interest rates is taken." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 4:25 p.m. EDT (2025 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Friday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.5175      1.5216   1.5212\par   