\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Morning: C$ Down, But Mkt Wary Of More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 15:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar is down slightly but its movements remain fairly constrained Monday morning as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players wonder about the possibility of another massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly and dramatically in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Friday morning, selling hundreds of millions of U.S. dollars in an effort to re-introduce some resiliency into the battered Canadian unit. \par \par \uc2  The bank's sudden move has made some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players wary about another \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move, market watchers say. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5218 at 9:30 a.m. EDT (1330 GMT), from C$1.5216 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) and from C$1.5212 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  "I think there's a newfound respect for the bank," said Tom Benfer, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the Bank of Montreal in New York. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciated going into the Bank of Canada's 9:00 a.m. EDT (1300 GMT) rate hike window, and then declined afterwards, reflecting continued expectations in some quarters that the bank may still raise interest rates in defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Like many other market watchers, Benfer believes an interest rate defense is unlikely at this point. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. dollar level of C$1.5250 is critical for the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he suggested. If the U.S. reaches that level, it will set the stage for a renewed push to C$1.5300. \par \par \uc2  "What's going to be crucial going forward, I think, is the next time we see the hand of officialdom," Benfer said. "They don't know if he's going to come back in . . . and punish the market." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 9:30 a.m. EDT (1330 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Friday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.5218      1.5216   1.5212\par    CDN/DEM     1.1695      1.1170   1.1701\par    CDN/YEN     96.20       96.20    96.11\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1333GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8a06rj8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
