\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Repeated  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 16:28\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market repeatedly Monday morning,\par selling U.S. dollars at various levels beginning around\par C$1.5230, said traders in Toronto.\par    In a move similar to Friday's massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  began pouring U.S. dollars into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par markets at various levels at around 10:00 a.m. EDT (1400\par GMT), pushing the U.S. dollar its starting point around\par C$1.5230 to C$1.5152 a few minutes later.\par    It was at C$1.5178 at 10:24 a.m. EDT (1424 GMT).\par    The action came much earlier than the bank's normal\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level, which would have been around C$1.5290.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's usual, unofficial policy is to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets after intraday moves in either\par direction of 70 ticks or more in order to contain\par volatility. The U.S. dollar closed at C$1.5218 on Friday.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seemed intent on following up Friday's\par dramatic move, which also came before the normal\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trigger.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market sources were unable to comment on the\par size of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  immediately after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's commenced its sales Monday morning. Friday's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was said to be massive, encompassing hundreds\par of millions of U.S. dollars.\par    Friday's move started at a U.S. dollar level of C$1.5350\par and pushed the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down to C$1.5115, although it\par rebounded to C$1.5218 by Friday's close.\par    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market players believe the dramatic\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves are an effort to change the one-way flow\par of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent weeks.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been under severe downward pressure\par recently, and has been driven deeper into uncharted\par territory for most of the past few weeks.\par    Analysts blame the recent spate of weakness in the\par Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the low commodity prices and global\par uncertainties stemming from the renewed economic and\par financial turmoil in Asia, as negative yield spreads between\par Canada and the U.S., and a recent string of soft Canadian\par economic indicators.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-10-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1028EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8a01xje\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\pi