\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Slides Vs Mark, Flat Vs Yen; Quiet Trading \b0\par\par\uc2  By Paul Podolsky \par \uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 22:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar barely moved against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, although it slid against the Deutsche mark late in the New York trading session. \par \par \uc2  Traders couldn't cite any one reason for the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, although it may have resulted from thin trading and a tepid performance by U.S. stocks, some said. \par \par \uc2  Fresh information relevant to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would seem largely dollar bullish, however. The failure of a Japanese copy machine maker, Mita Industrial Co., a 38% rise in Japanese personal bankruptcies and the denunciation of Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi's economic plans by opposition lawmakers all boded poorly for the yen, traders and analysts agreed. \par \par \uc2  Also, according to a report in Monday's edition of the German weekly Focus magazine, Federal Reserve chairman Alan Greenspan told a top German opposition politician that Japanese banking sector is "fragile." \par \par \uc2  David Ogg, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson Bank in New York said Y147.00 remains a key figure. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the ruble sank, as Russian stocks fell 9% and government debt yields rose. Tumultuous trading in Russia often drags the mark lower against the dollar, though that didn't happen Monday. Talk that the ruble will devalue persisted. \par \par \uc2  In trading elsewhere, the Canadian dollar rose after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sunk to historic lows against the dollar in recent weeks. Late in New York, the dollar was at C$1.5165, off from C$1.5230 prior to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but up from C$1.5152 immediately following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling. \par \par \uc2  Late afternoon in New York, the dollar was trading at Y146.18, flat from Y146.25 Friday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at DEM1.7755, down from 1.7803 Friday. Sterling was trading at $1.6353, up from 1.6295. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 10-08-98 \par \par \uc2  2027GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 20714 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8a06s96\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
