\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  -3: Repeat  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Expected \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 1998\par 20:26\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Instead, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be gambling that a more\par proactive stance on its behalf in favor of the Canadian\par dollar, combined with an expected improvement in many\par economic data indicators starting in August, may be enough to\par turn the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's downward momentum around.\par    "The combination of surprise \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and better-than-expected jobs data in July might\par start to improve sentiment towards the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,"\par said Rob Palombi, an economist at Standard and Poor's MMS in\par Toronto. "I think we'll see the bank hold off on raising\par rates."\par    Observers say that for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to work decisively in\par favor of the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , it may have to be repeated\par several times over the near term so that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  players\par become convinced of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's resolve.\par    "What's obviously going to happen is that come Monday\par morning when the Bank doesn't raise rates is the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar\par guys will start going at it again," said David Ebata, senior\par Canadian market analyst at Techdata in Boston. "If the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gets much above C$1.5200, everybody's going to start\par looking for the Bank of Canada to come in again."\par    Ebata said the Friday's style of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely\par a "good trial balloon" for a revised \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy\par aimed at checking the U.S. dollar's recent overpowering\par momentum, and it will likely have to make at least several\par reappearances for it to be fully effective.\par    "If the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gets much above C$1.5200,\par everybody's going to start looking for the Bank of Canada to\par come in again," he said. "If he's not there, then we're right\par back where we were early Friday. But I would guarantee that\par he'll be there on Monday."\par    - By Paul Evans; (416) 943-7811; paul-r evans@dowjones.ca\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-07-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1426EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4238 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8701wsb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
