\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  C$  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not Seen Presaging Rate Move \b0\par\par\uc2  By Paul Evans \par \uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 1998\par 20:10\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--Untypically massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par support of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's battered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday isn't likely to be followed by a hike in domestic\par interest rates, analysts say.\par    With the decline in the Canadian dollar threatening to\par spiral out of control recently, the Bank of Canada jolted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  players Friday morning with several large waves of\par U.S. dollar-selling.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's actions drove the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down\par through a 250-point range in one of the widest, most volatile\par intraday swings in value ever seen for the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Beginning at a U.S. dollar level of about C$1.5345,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  selling of U.S. dollars pushed the U.S. unit\par down as far as C$1.5115 in the space of only 35 minutes prior\par to 10 a.m. EDT (1400 GMT) before the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recovered\par its footing and started moving back towards the C$1.5200\par level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Apart from the size and frequency of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par the bank's move was atypical and precedent-setting in that it\par began in advance of its usual threshold for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's unofficial policy has been to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  only when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves 70 ticks in either\par direction from the previous day's close. With the U.S. dollar\par having closed at C$1.5294 Thursday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par normally have been anticipated only as it approached\par C$1.5360.\par    Friday's developments definitely represent a change in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy away from the previous mode of\par symmetrical \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the basis of 70-tick moves,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  players say.\par    "The bank was atypically aggressive, and they drew a line\par in the sand today, no question," said Stephen Wateridge,\par managing director of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the Canadian\par Imperial Bank of Commerce. "It's clearly the first sign of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that didn't take place at your standard 70-75\par points, and that's a signal."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  08-07-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1410EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4238 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8701wrx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
