\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Heavy  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Reported \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 1998\par 15:50\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market repeatedly and heavily Friday morning, selling U.S. dollars in an effort to smooth out trading action, said a trader in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  Traders reported the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at several different levels, ranging from C$1.5345, C$1.5350 and C$1.5355, and described the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as extremely heavy. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar dropped significantly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reached levels around C$1.5230 shortly after the intensive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2  It rose back up afterwards, and was at C$1.5270 at 9:40 a.m. EDT (1340 GMT), but then tumbling again in response to the sustained selling of U.S. dollars by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was at C$1.5159 at 9:46 a.m. EDT (1346 GMT), and was showing continued volatility. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was both heavy and premature, since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unofficial policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after intraday moves in either direction of 70 ticks or more in order to contain volatility. Since the U.S. dollar closed at C$1.5294 on Thursday, the normal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level would have been around C$1.5365. \par \par \uc2  Because the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was both extensive and early, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market sources are speculating that the Bank of Canada will follow it up with an interest rate increase on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar has been under severe downward pressure in recent sessions, but the sell off intensified dramatically Thursday, with the U.S. dollar moving to C$1.5294 at Thursday's close from C$1.5174 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Thursday's sharp decline also triggered repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts blame the recent spate of weakness in the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the low commodity prices and global uncertainties stemming from the renewed economic and financial turmoil in Asia. \par \par \uc2  A recent string of weak Canadian economic indicators has also exacerbated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's problems, market watchers say. \par \par \uc2  Some market watchers say sustained negative yield spreads between Canada and the U.S. are also a key reason for the Canadian dollar's weakness. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-07-98 \par \par \uc2  0950EDT \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8701wgs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
