\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian dollar plunges as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Masaru Sato \par \uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1998\par 20:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, Aug 6 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar slid further down a long slope on Thursday morning, dropping almost one full cent in value against the U.S. dollar to another record low. \par \par \uc2  The drop came despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The record low was about C$1.53 to the U.S. dollar, which meant one Canadian dollar was worth about 65.4 U.S. cents. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada is watching to see if the present weakness in Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bond and stock markets is causing a dangerous loss of investor confidence. \par \par \uc2  North American stock markets have been bearish this week and the Toronto stock market was down again at midday. Canada's long-term government bond prices fell nearly a full point. \par \par \uc2  All this makes for a brave, or fearful, new world for traders and forecasters. \par \par \uc2  "I think we are in virgin territory here, so every big figure is a target. I think C$1.53 (65.40 U.S. cents) is my first resistance (for the U.S. dollar)," said Martin Autotte, technical analyst at CIBC Wood Gundy Securities. \par \par \uc2  "We've already come up 100 points very quickly today, and I think that should put a cap on the Canadian dollar's weakness for the week," he said. "Going into next week, we're definitely targeting C$1.54 (64.9 U.S. cents)." \par \par \uc2  The markets are bracing just in case the Bank of Canada raises interest rates to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but a general consensus among economists is that the best policy for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to hold off raising rates unless the weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  starts to undermine economic activity. \par \par \uc2  Higher borrowing costs for firms and consumers at a time of global uncertainty could further depress consumer and business confidence. \par \par \uc2  More importantly, economists predicted that a rate increase alone may not be powerful enough to turn around the marked downtrend in the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  Financial markets are awaiting the release on Friday of U.S. and Canadian employment data for July to confirm a slower pace of economic growth in Canada and whether the U.S. labour market is exerting inflationary pressure on the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  Then there is the Monica Lewinsky factor. Her testimony in the White House sex and perjury scandal, if it threatens the security of U.S. President Bill Clinton in his job, could suggest a risk for holding U.S. dollar assets. \par \par \uc2  ((Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8601rp7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
