\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Afternoon: C$ Dives Sharply In 'Disorderly' Market \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1998\par 22:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar ended down sharply against the U.S. dollar Thursday, in a pronounced sell-off that knocked the Canadian unit down more than 100 ticks from the previous day's official close at C$1.5174. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5288 at 4:52 p.m. EDT (2052 GMT), from C$1.5212 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) and from C$1.5185 late Wednesday. It briefly hit C$1.5300 late in Thursday afternoon before retreating. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  was reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily and repeatedly Thursday, beginning at the C$1.5245 level, in an effort to moderate the pressure against the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at each subsequent five-tick advance by the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  While the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been staggering under intense selling pressure since early July, Thursday marked one of its largest single-session declines in recent memory, and analysts were at a loss to pinpoint a single reason for the fall. \par \par \uc2  Some said the market was swept late Wednesday by an unfounded rumor of a potentially destabilizing autumn election in the province of Quebec, which carried over to weaken the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in overnight trading in international markets, with a carryover on Thursday in North America. \par \par \uc2  "That rumor was enough to push the U.S. dollar over C$1.5200, and the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  just could not come back," said Jim Webber, managing director of fixed-income research at Toronto Dominion Securities. "It set us up very weakly from a technical standpoint today." \par \par \uc2  While there is nothing new from a fundamental standpoint for the Canadian dollar, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers say momentum for the U.S. dollar has built up significantly over the past several sessions, raising the likelihood of further significant gains against its Canadian counterpart in upcoming sessions. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 06-08-98 \par \par \uc2  2058GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8606oii\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
