\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Morning: C$ Down; Further Fall Past C$1.5240 Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1998\par 15:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar is pushing farther into new record low territory early Thursday, having fallen past another psychological resistance level at a U.S. dollar level of C$1.5200 overnight. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5235 at 9:40 a.m. EDT (1340 GMT), from C$1.5212 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) and from C$1.5185 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gathered momentum late in Wednesday's North American session, and then pushed effortlessly past the previous all-time spot high of C$1.5190 in overnight trading in international markets. \par \par \uc2  It stalled briefly early in Thursday's North American session, before regaining momentum on several large orders from offshore accounts selling Canadian dollars. \par \par \uc2  "Today is really just a continuation of the trend," said a trader at a major Canadian bank. "There was a couple of big orders selling Canada early this morning, and the speculator types have also been active." \par \par \uc2  After having recorded an official close of C$1.5174 Wednesday, the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already fallen just short of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's designated trigger level for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unofficial policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after intraday moves in either direction of 70 ticks or more in order to contain volatility. \par \par \uc2  Local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers expect the U.S. dollar to move past its short-term target of C$1.5240 Thursday and begin building a new base of support for an eventual move to C$1.5300. \par \par \uc2  In related developments, the government announced Thursday that Canada's monetary reserves, including foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , jumped $2.55 billion in July to $22.52 billion. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 9:40 a.m. EDT (1340 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Wednesday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.5235      1.5212   1.5185\par    CDN/DEM     1.1585      1.1624   1.1646\par    CDN/YEN     94.88       94.98    94.83\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1342GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8606nnt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
