\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: U.S. Dlr Now At C$1.5115 \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 19:10\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday afternoon, selling U.S.\par dollars at C$1.5130 in an effort to smooth out trading\par action, said a trader in Toronto.\par    The U.S. dollar leveled off briefly after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and was hovering at C$1.5115 at 1:01 p.m. EDT\par (1701 GMT).\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's unofficial policy is to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets after intraday moves in either direction\par of 70 ticks or more in order to contain volatility. The\par U.S. dollar closed at C$1.5063 on Thursday.\par    The Canadian dollar has been under severe downward\par pressure in recent sessions, having fallen to consecutive\par record lows in nine of the last 10 trading sessions.\par    Analysts say the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has fundamental\par weaknesses stemming from low commodity prices and global\par uncertainties stemming from the renewed economic and\par financial turmoil in Asia, as well as from sustained\par negative yield spreads between Canada and the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    But many market watchers say the pressure on the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has taken on a more speculative tone lately, with\par many believing it can be pushed lower without risking a\par defensive raising of interest rates by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par response.\par    The intense pressure on the Canadian dollar is expected\par to last until the pressures originating in Asia relent, or\par the Bank of Canada raises interest rates to defend the\par embattled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  07-31-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1310EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du7v01uu3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
