\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Afternoon: C$ Slips Lower, Bk of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 22:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar ended significantly lower Friday, as the U.S. dollar pushed through the landmark level of C$1.5100 and into the uncharted territory beyond. \par \par \uc2  The size of the move prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with sold off U.S. dollars midway through the session to slow down the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5120 at 4:21 p.m. EDT (2021 GMT), from C$1.5036 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) and from C$1.5059 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  It reached C$1.5130 shortly before 1:00 p.m. EDT (1700 GMT), setting a new all-time high and prompting a round of U.S. dollar selling at that level by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the U.S. dollar moves 70 ticks or more in either direction against the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to restrict market volatility. \par \par \uc2  Some market sources attributed early downward pressure on the Canadian unit to the news that Canadian gross domestic product declined 0.2% in May, coupled with the fact that U.S. GDP increased 1.4% in the second quarter. \par \par \uc2  But others questioned whether the figures had sustained impact. \par \par \uc2  Rob Palombi, financial markets analyst at Standard & Poor's MMS, said with low U.S. inflation clearly keeping the U.S. Federal Reserve Board on the sidelines, the growth differential between Canada and the U.S. should not necessarily be a big source of pressure for the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  A New York-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed the same script on Friday as it has for the last few weeks. \par \par \uc2  "It's been the same story we've run into for the last two weeks or so," he said. "The market buys Canada into the (Bank of Canada's interest rate window), and when the bank does nothing, we just move the other way." \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 31-07-98 \par \par \uc2  2026GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7v06hfm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
