\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Morning: C$ Down, Trends Lower On Weak May GDP Data \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 15:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar is down against the U.S. dollar in active trading early Friday, after the early morning release of weak Canadian May GDP figures combined with a strong second quarter U.S. GDP report provided a worst-case scenario for the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5075 at 9:40 a.m. EDT (1340 GMT), from C$1.5036 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) and from C$1.5059 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said selling pressure on the Canadian unit was relatively restrained after the 8:30 a.m. EDT (1230 GMT) release of the GDP data leading into the Bank of Canada's 'window' for raising interest rates near 9 a.m. \par \par \uc2  But when it was clear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would again sit tight on interest rates, a flood of sell orders drove the Canadian dollar towards its all-time low of C$1.5092 seen in overnight trading in international markets. \par \par \uc2  While the Canadian unit pulled back slightly to hover around the C$1.5070 level, market watchers say early Friday action reaffirmed that the uptrend for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still operative, and that expectations are for the U.S. unit to continue on towards the C$1.5100 mark. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. dollar will likely brush up against Friday's set limit for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a Montreal-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist. "There's been a tendency recently to go up just short of those levels, consolidate, and then the next day take out that level." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unofficial policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to contain volatility whenever the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves 70 ticks in either direction from the previous day's close. The bank's official Thursday close for the Canadian dollar was C$1.5063. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 9:40 a.m. EDT (1340 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Thursday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.5075      1.5036    1.5059\par    CDN/DEM     1.1814      1.1823    1.1817\par    CDN/YEN     95.72       95.90     95.41\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 31-07-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1343GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7v06gjh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
