\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Afternoon -2: U.S. Dlr Seen Targetting C$1.5100 \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1998\par 22:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  While the Canadian dollar had trended slowly lower throughout Wednesday's session as the U.S. dollar regained strength versus the yen, late afternoon dealings pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the brink of the C$1.5075 level thought to be the trigger for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's general policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever the exchange rate moves 70 ticks in either direction from the previous day's close. \par \par \uc2  With Tuesday's abortive rally now seemingly exhausted, most believe that barring unforseen developments, the U.S. dollar will now resume its pattern of making moderate daily gains against the Canadian unit, with the C$1.5100 level now in sight. \par \par \uc2  "C$1.5100 is in the cards unfortunately, though we might fall back a bit first," said Wateridge. "Clearly, the market is going to continually try to test the Bank of Canada's resolve." \par \par \uc2  Some traders said a move to between C$1.5080 and C$1.5100 is possible Thursday or Friday, especially if Friday's May Canadian GDP data shows unexpected weakness, or if Thursday's release of U.S. second-quarter employment cost index reaffirms expectations of tighter monetary conditions down the road for that nation. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 4:25 p.m. EDT (2025 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Tuesday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.5055      1.5000    1.5004\par    CDN/DEM     1.1770      1.1822    1.1797\par    CDN/YEN     94.55       94.69     94.05\pa