\par\par \b \uc2  No reprieve in sight as Canada dollar falls again. \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 1998\par 23:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, July 27 (Reuters) - Canada's dollar continued its swoon on Monday, hitting more record lows, and traders and economists expected it to weaken still further in the absence any supporting news. \par \par \uc2  That means Canadians will have to keep on paying more than one and a half Canadian dollars to get one U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The new trading low was C$1.5053 (US$0.6643) against the U.S dollar, reached in afternoon trade. The Canadian dollar ended official North American trade at C$1.5032 (US$0.6652), a record closing low. \par \par \uc2  Despite vague market expectations of some action, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and has held off raising key lending rates as a means of attracting investors to Canadian assets. \par \par \uc2  The slide in the Canadian dollar has been constant but orderly. \par \par \uc2  Much of Canada's weakness derives from soft commodities prices as the nation still relies on exports of oil, gas, and farm and forest products for a substantial part of national income. \par \par \uc2  In the eyes of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders, there are few fundamental factors supporting Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment. \par \par \uc2  Economic indicators have shown signs of a slower pace of growth in Canada, and investors tend to choose U.S. dollar assets as a safe-haven when uncertainty persists, as it does now in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar is on a downtrend against the German mark, while climbing against the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  ((Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7r000he\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
