\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Canada Dlr Breaches Key C$1.5000 Level \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 1998\par 23:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere Monday, the Canadian dollar sank past the psychologically important level of C$1.5000 to a U.S. dollar. The next target level of C$1.6000 will be attainable, especially if the dollar manages to extend its gains against the yen, said Bank of America's Nickerson. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was quoted at C$1.5035, down from an intraday high of C$1.5053, but up from C$1.4990 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accommodated the the weak trend seen in the Canadian dollar. However, "if the market starts to question if it is benign neglect as opposed to a policy," then the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to show it is paying attention, said Nickerson. \par \par \uc2  Other so-called commodity-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened against the dollar as well. The Australian dollar and the New Zealand dollar both fell on the back of a weak yen Monday. \par \par \uc2  The same trend- tracking the yen- was seen in a majority of the Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, with the exception of the Indonesian rupiah, which gained nearly 2% on the day. The rupiah broke the psychologically important level of IDR14,000 to a dollar after two protest demonstrations remained peaceful. \par \par \uc2  In intraday trading Monday, the U.S. dollar fell to IDR13,700, but has since recouped those losses and was trading near IDR14,100 late in New York, unchanged from Friday's levels. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the focus is now on the two-day meeting of countries which lend money to Indonesia to take place in Paris later this week . The donor countries are expected to increase significantly the amount of loans they provide to Indonesia this year from US$5.3 billion last year. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 27-07-98 \par \par \uc2  2129GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7r06b4p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
