\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar opens flat, stuck in tight slot. \b0\par\par\uc2 983 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 1998\par 16:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.4930/1.4975\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.4964\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US$ SUPPORT 1.4890  RESISTANCE 1.5035 HIGH 1.4970 LOW 1.4945\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4953 HIGH 1.4970\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4962\par PREV CLOSE  1.4956 LOW  1.4945\tab HIGH 1.4955 LOW 1.4944\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FRIDAY, JULY 24\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL, ACTIVITY: MODERATE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada's dollar opened little changed at C$1.4953 (US$0.6688),\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moving in tight range. *Overnight high for U.S dollar was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limited to C$1.4970 (US$0.6680), record low level for Canada\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par marked Thursday here. *U.S. dollar taking time before testing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $1.5000 (US$0.6667) as oscillators show slightly overbought\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollars. *Canada on downtrend against mark and yen. *Japan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ruling Liberal Democrats elected bland Foreign Minister Obuchi\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as new party leader, who will succeed outgoing Prime Minister\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hashimoto after being approved by parliament in late July or\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par early August. *His election already priced into markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Downside risk for yen and Japanese equities is any\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par disappointment over pace of banking, tax reform debates and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par implementation. *Greenspan testimony to House Banking Committee\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on derivatives at 1000 EDT/1400 GMT, and Q&A on same topic at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about 1100 EDT/1500 GMT today.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, July 24 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar opened little changed at C$1.4953 (US$0.6688), moving in a tight range, but remained weak against other key \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The overnight high for the U.S dollar was limited to C$1.4970 (US$0.6680), a record low level for the Canadian unit set on Thursday during North American trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar is marking time before testing the next key resistance of $1.5000 (US$0.6667) as oscillators show U.S. dollars are slightly overbought. Traders have become more cautious about testing that level, fearing the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would step in with decisive market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the chart, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is on a downtrend against the mark, and generally against the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, the Canadian unit continued to slip to 1.1899 marks from 1.1926 marks at the previous close here, the lowest level since mid-January 1997, when Canada was recovering from a bottom. Canada edged down to 93.81 yen from 94.35 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan's ruling Liberal Democrats elected bland Foreign Minister Keizo Obuchi overnight as new party leader. He will succeed outgoing Prime Minister Hashimoto after winning parliamentary approval in late July or early August.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par His selection came as no surprise as it had already been priced into markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the coming weeks and months, a downside risk for the yen and Japanese equities is any disappointment over the pace of banking and tax system reform debate and implementation. Younger ruling party members have threatened to secede if the new leader fails to help pull the nation's economy out of its worst post-war recession.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Whatever the composition of the new cabinet, Japan will continue to use its traditional method of making decisions by seeking consensus through haggling among political factions and bureaucrats.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan is scheduled to testify at the House Banking Committee on derivatives at 1000 EDT/1400 GMT, and answer questions on the same topic at about 1100 EDT/1500 GMT today.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Greenspan's comments pointing to cyclical price corrections in the market in his key congressional testimony triggered heavy selling in North American stock markets earlier this week. His stance on monetary policy still appears to be biased towards tightening to prevent any inflationary pressure on the economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After seeing no action by Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par daily money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost the Canadian dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par traders sold local dollars to a new record trading low of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par C$1.4981 (US$0.6675) in morning trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was stable after that action with traders seen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par squaring their positions ahead of the weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Speculation for a key lending rate increase by the bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par comes and goes. The Bank of Canada has resisted occasional\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market demand for a higher interest rate as a means of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attracting investors with higher returns on Canadian dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The time for window (for money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) past, it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par came and went, they didn't hike as I think a lot of Canadians\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had expected, and Americans were looking for a bit of a rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hike today for some reason," one trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He noted stop-loss buying of U.S. dollars at C$1.4980\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (US$0.6676) and stop-loss selling at C$1.4930/35\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (US$0.6698/0.6696), a support level for the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's natural that people are trying to square up or get\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par out if we break that," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Uncertainty also persisted as some option-related moves are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par anticipated as players hedge their positions by exercising or\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not exercising their rights to buy or sell dollars at certain\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par levels in the future.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think there are some option (contracts), it will be only\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par natural that some option triggers around the C$1.5000 level,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par whether or not some guys would be selling at that level or some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par guys trying to buy remains to be seen," the trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Key economic indicators for next week (hit ECI/US + F9 for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a full list for U.S. data)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday, July 29\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. June durable goods forecast at -0.4 percent after -2.6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in May.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday, July 30\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. second quarter employment cost index seen at +0.8\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent after +0.7 percent in Q1\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. second quarter gross domestic product (GDP) +0.2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent after +5.4 percent in Q1.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada's May GDP (forecast to come later).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7o005wf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
