\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar ends weak, but off new trading low. \b0\par\par\uc2 842 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1998\par 22:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.4930/1.4990\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.4952\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US$ SUPPORT 1.4925  RESISTANCE 1.5035 HIGH 1.4966 LOW 1.4950\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4962 HIGH 1.4971\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4962\par PREV CLOSE  1.4953 LOW  1.4933\tab HIGH 1.4965 LOW 1.4952\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THURSDAY, JULY 23\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL, ACTIVITY: MODERATE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada's dollar ended little changed at C$1.4956 (US$0.6686), a record low\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closing level but off a new trading low of C$1.4971 (US$0.6680) hit earlier\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par today. *Earlier CAD rose on rumours that U.S. Fed was selling T-bills to raise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par funds for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Bank of Japan and Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars. *Market players later sold CAD a bit, thinking BOC in no need to raise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par liquidity that way. *CAD in consolidation as two-way corporate demand emerged,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but C$1.5000 (US$0.6667) still next target. *U.S. dollar dipped on rumour Fed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par selling T-bills for BOJ, but remained steady in afternoon. *USD rose above 142\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen overseas on growing concern over Japan's ability to fix financial problems.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Moody's put Japan's Aaa debt raging under review for possible downgrade. *Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Canada staying quiet, trying to avoid any deterioration of CAD by commenting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on market. *BOC looking at weak commodities prices, Canada's exports, and low\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation. *BOC's monitoring investor confidence, but its aim appears not to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fight flow of exchange rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, July 23 (Reuters) - Canada's battered dollar resisted selling pressure most of the day, but ended at a record closing low of C$1.4956 (US$0.6686) on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That was still firmer than a new trading low of C$1.4971 (US$0.6680) set in morning trade before unfounded rumours gave the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a temporary shot in the arm.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian dollar rose on rumours that the U.S. Federal Reserve was selling treasury bills to raise funds for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Bank of Japan and Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell U.S. dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market players later sold back Canadian dollars slightly, realising that Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would have of no need of the help of its U.S. counterpart to raise liquidity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It wasn't breaking the C$1.4940 level convincingly so people turned around and took back their short (U.S) dollar positions," one trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The pace of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's 19-week slide has slowed and it is stuck in a tight range as both buy and sell orders emerged from corporate customers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some players have predicted that the U.S. dollar will hit the next target of C$1.5000 (US$0.6667) by the end of the week, but traders now think it might take a little more time.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar was steady this afternoon after rising above 142 yen overseas on growing concern over Japan's ability to fix its financial problems and jump-start the economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The latest shock to the Asian markets came overnight from credit rating agency Moody's Investors Service, which has put Japan's top-notch Aaa debt rating under review for a possible downgrade, an unprecedented move for Japan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Uncertainty about Japan also persisted ahead of Friday's election of the nation's ruling party leader, who will become the next prime minister unless any large-scale defectors undermine the party's majority in the powerful Lower House of parliament.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, the Canadian unit, after a rebound, ended the session down at 1.1926 marks from 1.1954 marks at the previous close here. Canada gave up earlier gains and was flat at 94.35 yen after 94.34 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Above C$1.5000 is uncharted territory and hard to project trend lines, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the next price objective after that level is  C$1.5033, based on recent moves,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said Katherine Beattie, senior technical analyst at Standard & Poor's MMS.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of Canada has maintained its silence, trying to avoid any\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deterioration of the exchange rate by commenting on the market, particularly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after Prime Minister Jean Chretien came under fire for saying last week that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the weak local dollar was good for Canada's exports and tourism.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bank is looking at soft commodities prices and resulting weakness in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada's exports, and a low inflation rate, which has worked as a buffer for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It is monitoring investor confidence in Canadian dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par assets, but its aim appears not to fight the flow of exchange rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Friday, Japan's ruling Liberal Democrats will cast their votes, starting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at 1400 JST/0500 GMT/0100 EDT, and the results of the first vote will be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par announced at around 1450 JST/0550 GMT/0150 EDT. If there is a winner, he will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hold a news conference at 1600 JST/0700 GMT/0300 on the same day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7n00b71\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
