\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar ends flat, range-bound pre Greenspan. \b0\par\par\uc2 700 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1998\par 22:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.4860/1.4900\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.4875\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US$ SUPPORT 1.4815  RESISTANCE 1.5035 HIGH 1.4881 LOW 1.4865\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4869 HIGH 1.4892\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4862\par PREV CLOSE  1.4884 LOW  1.4862\tab HIGH 1.4888 LOW 1.4863\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MONDAY, JULY 20\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL, ACTIVITY: MODERATE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada dollar ended around C$1.4888 (US$0.6717) in range-stuck\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade. *Traders tested the U.S. dollar's topside at C$1.4892\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (US$0.6715) just before close. *In early trade, the market ignored\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par potentially bearish news that Canada's May wholesale trade was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par down 1.2 pct m/m against consensus forecast of 0.5 pct rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *It posted lowest y/y rise (+5.1 pct) since Feb 1996. *Market awaits Greenspan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Humphrey-Hawkins testimony Tuesday and Wednesday. *Japan ruling party leader\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par election Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, July 20 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar ended flat at C$1.4887 (US$0.6717) on Monday after moving in a tight range and ahead of key testimony by the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders tested the topside of the U.S. dollar at C$1.4892 (US$0.6715) just before the close. Earlier buying of Canada was limited to C$1.4862 (US$0.6729).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading was relatively light and driven by technical factors, ignoring another piece of weak domestic economic data that suggests a slower pace of economic growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market is in neutral gear after seeing no follow-through selling of Canadian unit. It scratched a record trading low of C$1.4918 (US$0.6703) on Friday in technical moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, the Canadian dollar recovered from initial selling and rose to 1.1967 marks from 1.1960 marks at the previous close here, but it was still at its lowest level since mid-January 1997. Canada continued to slip to 93.24 yen from 93.66 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Both the German and Japanese units have recently been bid up against the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada's May wholesale trade fell 1.2 percent month on month against consensus forecast of a 0.5-percent rise, and posted the lowest year-on-year rise of 5.1 percent since February 1996.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think it falls in the place, with a lot of people saying, where some of the recent numbers have shown that the North American economy is slowing a bit, and the wholesale trade number further reinforced that voice," said Reid Farrill, executive director, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at CIBC Wood Gundy Securities. "It didn't come as a surprise, but it was surprisingly low."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market is awaiting any hint for the future course of U.S. monetary policy from Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan, who is scheduled to discusses the U.S. economy during his semi-annual Humphrey-Hawkins congressional testimony on Tuesday and Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The last time Greenspan testified, on June 10, North American bond prices\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par surged on his balanced comments and on prevailing flight-to-quality capital\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par flows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On that day, the Canadian dollar came under speculative\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par selling, which prompted Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollars for U.S. dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At that time, Greenspan told the Joint Economic Committee of Congress the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Federal Reserve might have to raise interest rates if demand were to continue\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to exhibit few signs of abating noticeably, but that there was no need for a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tighter monetary policy to cool off the economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market is also awaiting Friday's election of Japan's new ruling party\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par leader, who will succeed Ryutaro Hashimoto as Japan's prime minister.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Former government spokesman and veteran backroom fixer\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Seiroku Kajiyama, who has proposed drastic banking reform,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appears to be ahead of the other two contenders in the latest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par poll of party members.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The mark has been gaining ground on growing optimism over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Russia's financial reforms.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Consensus forecasts for key economic indicators for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week of July 20:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday, July 21\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada May retail trade +0.4 percent (+1.0 percent in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par April)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7k00k3c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
