\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar opens flat, trade data little impact. \b0\par\par\uc2 844 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 1998\par 14:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.4860/1.4920\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.4882\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US$ SUPPORT 1.4815  RESISTANCE 1.5035 HIGH 1.4898 LOW 1.4883\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4884 HIGH 1.4898\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4880\par PREV CLOSE  1.4890 LOW  1.4871\tab HIGH 1.4894 LOW 1.4878\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FRIDAY, JULY 16\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL, ACTIVITY: MODERATE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada dollar opened flat at C$1.4884 (US$0.6719), moving in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tight range. *Dollar/Canada little changed after 0830 EDT/1230\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT release of Canada's May trade data, which showed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par larger-than-forecast trade surplus of C$1.67 billion after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par C$1.20 billion in April. *Economists had forecast C$1.22\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion for May. *Yen steady to firmer vs U.S. dollar on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growing hope that Japan will fix financial problems sooner than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par later.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, July 17 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar opened flat at C$1.4884 (US$0.6719) on Friday and hovered around that level before the market tested the topside of the U.S. dollar again.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was no immediate market reaction to the release of Canada's May trade data, which showed a bigger-than-expected C$1.67 billion in trade surplus after C$1.20 billion in April. Economists had forecast C$1.22 billion for May.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This is supportive of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , there is no question there," Randall Powley, senior economist at Scotia Capital Markets, told Reuters Television. "It's a supportive move, although most of the weakness in the Canadian dollar hasn't been domestically driven... so we can't say this is going to be lasting support for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A recent spate of weak domestic economic data have weighed on the battered Canadian dollar against the U.S. dollar. But Canada has been under downward pressure from slow recovery in commodities prices, which was brought on by slack Asian demand. Capital has also been flowing into U.S. dollar assets as they maintain safe-haven status.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, the Canadian dollar was little changed at 1.1997 marks after falling to this level on Thursday, which was unseen since April 1997. Canada fell to 93.63 yen from 94.03 yen at the previous close here.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen was steady to firmer against the U.S. dollar on growing hopes that Japan will fix its economic and banking problems sooner than later as candidates for the next premiership disclose plans to fight the recession and cure reform the financial system, one factor hampering path to quick turnaround in business and consumer sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The Canadian unit, which has been sliding constantly for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the past four months, touched a record trading low of C$1.4915\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (US$0.6705) this morning as modest U.S. dollar buying emerged.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     This move was largely anticipated as traders held their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par breath for a remote possibility of Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raising a key lending rate at the 0900 EDT/1300 GMT window of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and found that there was no support\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from the money side.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Within minutes, Canada's dollar quickly recovered to around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the opening level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has staged occasional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to smooth out fluctuations, but has held off\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raising interest rates to defend the value of the local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think they have appropriate policy. The economy is in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reasonable shape, although growth numbers are more mixed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lately. That suggests they shouldn't be in a tightening\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par position. There's certainly no inflation pressure on the bank,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Powley said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada's consumer price index (CPI) showed tame inflation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Thursday, with overall CPI rising 1.0 percent year on year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in June after a 1.1-percent rise in May, and the core rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rising 1.0 percent after a 1.4 percent rise, both below\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has indicated that wider fluctuations of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary conditions are expected in Canada. It is watching\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par movements in the nation's short-term interest rates and the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's performance against other Group of 10 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par any signs of drastic easing in overall money conditions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was last seen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to slow the pace of depreciation on Wednesday, when the decline\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was precipitous.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The latest recent selling came from a string of weak\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic domestic economic data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On Wednesday, May manufacturing shipments showed a fall of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.0 percent after a revised drop of 0.7 percent in April, while\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economists had forecast a 0.6-percent rise. May car sales came\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in lower than expected, rising 1.1 percent after a 5.9-percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last week, the Canadian unit came under heavy selling after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the nation's employment fell for the second consecutive month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in June, by 35,900 to 14.24 million after a drop of 7,300 in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May. Housing starts dropped 4.6 percent in June, the third\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par straight month of declines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7h00nwn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
