\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar ends flat vs US dlr, down vs mark. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,146 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1998\par 21:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.4855/1.4920\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.4870\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US$ SUPPORT 1.4815  RESISTANCE 1.5035 HIGH 1.4891 LOW 1.4872\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4871 HIGH 1.4900\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4872\par PREV CLOSE  1.4890 LOW  1.4861\tab HIGH 1.4883 LOW 1.4870\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THURSDAY, JULY 16\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL, ACTIVITY: MODERATE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Canada's dollar ended little changed around C$1.4884 (US$0.6719) in subdued trading after opening a bit firmer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * CAD was propped by yen rise vs U.S. dollar, but optimism over Russia's economic reform triggered mark buying, sending CAD around 1.20 marks, lowest level since April 1997.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Market awaiting Canada's May trade surplus due out Friday (forecast: C$1.22 billion after C$1.20 billion in April), and nervously looking for any signal from Bank of Canada for rate action to defend CAD.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yen gained overnight on growing hopes in market that former chief cabinet secretary Kajiyama will win the race for the Japan PM's job, thus implementing drastic banking reform he's been proposing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Canada June CPI showed tame inflation, overall +1.0 pct y/y, core rate +1.0 y/y.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  <\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, July 16 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar ended around C$1.4884 (US$0.6719) on Thursday, weaker than the opening level, but showed some stability after Wednesday's steep decline to a record low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has suffered from bearish domestic economic data in recent trade, and the market is awaiting Canada's May trade surplus figures, due out Friday morning.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think what you will maybe see tomorrow is if there is a chance for this (market) to test the new high for (U.S.) dollar/Canada, they'll do it in the morning," one trader said. "And I think what you'll see in the afternoon is perhaps those who have been long (U.S.) dollars all week will take profits. So we may see some Canada buying coming into the market in the afternoon."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen's relative strength against the U.S. dollar helped cap a move to test the U.S. dollar's topside against Canada at C$1.4900 (US$0.6711).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the other hand, renewed buying of German marks on the notion that Russia is forging ahead with the economic reforms it promised in return for international loans was exerting downward pressure on Canada.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, the Canadian dollar broke through key support levels, falling to around 1.2000 marks, the lowest level since April 1997. It was quoted at 1.2086 marks at the previous close here.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollar/mark sentiment was swinging between optimistic and pessimistic as traders saw Russia's parliament approve some of Moscow's economic reform bills and reject others.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  extended overnight gains on growing expectations in the market that former chief cabinet secretary Seiroku Kajiyama will win the race for the leader of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) and succeed the outgoing prime minister, Ryutaro Hashimoto.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market favours the drastic banking reform plans Kajiyama has been proposing since he quit the cabinet of the previous Hashimoto government.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign Minister Keizo Obuchi, seen as a safe choice but lacking strong leadership, is still a frontrunner in the LDP election, which has been delayed by three days till July 24.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian unit fell to 94.03 yen after 94.37 yen on Wednesday in cross trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada's June consumer price index (CPI) showed tame inflation, but had little direct impact on the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overall CPI rose 1.0 percent year on year in June after a 1.1-percent rise in May, and the core rate (ex-food and energy prices) rose 1.0 percent from a year earlier after a 1.4 percent rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economists on average had forecast a 1.1-percent rise for all items and an increase of 1.3 percent for the core rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Although the Canadian dollar made a small rebound this morning, the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remained cautious about the outlook for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the Bank of Canada's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Trading had been nervous before the bank's money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  window at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0900 EDT/1300 GMT as some players speculated there would be an increase in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par key lending rate aimed at boosting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I guess you're concerned to the point where a weaker Canadian dollar could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raise import prices sufficiently to boost the inflation rate above the target\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par band, but that seems very unlikely at the moment because what's happening is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sure import prices are rising a bit from the U.S., but from products from Asia\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par we're seeing lower import prices," said Sal Guatieri, senior economist at Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Montreal.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He also told Reuters Television that Canada's economy is still operating\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par below capacity with a high unemployment rate, which is giving no wage cost\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If anything, you could make an argument that the Bank of Canada should be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cutting interest rates given the recent weak data, and all the negative shocks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Asia, falling commodities prices, and most simply because now inflation is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hovering a bit below the Bank of Canada's target band."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has indicated that a wider fluctuation of monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par conditions is expected in Canada. It is watching movements in the nation's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-term interest rates and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's performance against other Group of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for any signs of drastic easing in overall money conditions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian unit, which has been sliding constantly over the past four\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par months, hit a record trading low of C$1.4895 (US$0.6714) on Wednesday with\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slowing the pace of steep depreciation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The most recent selling came from a string of weak economic domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On Wednesday, May manufacturing shipments showed a fall of 1.0 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after a revised drop of 0.7 percent in April, while economists had forecast a 0.6-percent rise. May car sales came in lower than expected, rising 1.1 percent after a 5.9-percent rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last we]ek, the Canadian unit came under heavy selling pressure after the nation's employment fell for the second consecutive month in June, by 35,900 to 14.24 million, after a drop of 7,300 in May. Housing starts dropped 4.6 percent in June, the third straight month of declines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Consensus forecasts for key economic indicators for the rest of the week\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Friday, JULY 17\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Canada May trade surplus C$1.22 billion (April: C$1.20 billion)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    U.S. May trade deficit US$14.66 billion (April: US$14.46 billion)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7g00ts2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
