\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar opens firmer as U.S. dlr/yen drops. \b0\par\par\uc2 825 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1998\par 14:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.4855/1.4920\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.4870\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US$ SUPPORT 1.4815  RESISTANCE 1.5035 HIGH 1.4891 LOW 1.4872\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4871 HIGH 1.4891\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4872\par PREV CLOSE  1.4890 LOW  1.4868\tab HIGH 1.4883 LOW 1.4870\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THURSDAY, JULY 16\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL, ACTIVITY: MODERATE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada dollar opened a bit firmer at C$1.4871 (US$0.6724),\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par benefiting from U.S. dollar's fall vs yen. *Yen gained\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overnight on growing hopes in market that former chief cabinet\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sec Kajiyama will win race for Japan PM position, thus\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par implementing drastic banking reform he's been proposing. *This\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in turn hurting North American long bonds as safe-haven effect\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par subsides. *Canada June CPI showed tame inflation, overall +1.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pct y/y, core rate +1.0 y/y.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, July 16 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar on Thursday opened a bit firmer at C$1.4871 (US$0.6724), finally taking advantage of the yen's gain over the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, however, the Canadian unit continued to slip to 1.2025 marks from 1.2086 marks at the previous close here, and to 93.74 yen after 94.37 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  extended overnight gains on growing expectations in the market that former chief cabinet secretary Seiroku Kajiyama will win the race for the leader of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) to succeed the ougoing Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market favours drastic banking reform plans Kajiyama has been proposing since he quit the Cabinet member's post in the previous Hashimoto government.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign Minister Keizo Obuchi, seen as a safe choice but lacking strong leadership, is still a front runner in the LDP election, which has been delayed by three days until July 24.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada's June consumer price index (CPI) data showed inflation is tame, but had little direct impact on the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overall CPI rose 1.0 percent year on year in June after a 1.1-percent rise in May, and the core rate (ex-food and energy prices) rose 1.0 percent from a year earlier after a 1.4 percent rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economists on average had forecast a 1.1-percent rise for all items and an increase of 1.3 percent for the core rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although the Canadian dollar made a small rebound this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par morning, the market remained cautious about the outlook for the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the Bank of Canada's monetary policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I guess you're concerned to the point where a weaker\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canadian dollar could raise import prices sufficiently to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par boost the inflation rate above the target band, but that seems\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par very unlikely at the moment because what's happening is sure,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par import prices are rising a bit from the U.S., but from products\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Asia we're seeing lower import prices, said Sal Guatieri,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par senior economist at Bank of Montreal.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He also told Reuters Television that Canada's economy is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still operating below capacity with a high unemployment rate,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which is providing no wage cost pressures.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If anything, you could make an argument that the Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada should be cutting interest rates given the recent weak\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par data, and all the negative shocks from Asia, falling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par commodities prices, and most simply because now inflation is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hovering a bit below the Bank of Canada's target band.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has indicated that wider fluctuations of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary conditions are expected in Canada. It is watching\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par movements in the nation's short-term interest rates and the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's performance against other Group of 10 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par any signs of drastic easing in overall money conditions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian unit, which has been sliding constantly for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the past four months, hit a record trading low of C$1.4895\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (US$0.6714) on Wednesday with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slowing the pace of steep depreciation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The most recent bout of selling was prompted by a string of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weak economic domestic economic data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Wednesday, May manufacturing shipments showed a fall of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.0 percent after a revised drop of 0.7 percent in April, while\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economists had forecast a 0.6-percent rise. May car sales came\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in lower than expected, rising 1.1 percent after a 5.9-percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last week, the Canadian unit came under heavy selling after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the nation's employment fell for the second consecutive month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in June, by 35,900 to 14.24 million after a drop of 7,300 in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May. Housing starts dropped 4.6 percent in June, the third\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par straight month of declines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Consensus forecasts for key Canadian economic indicators\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the rest of the week:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday, JULY 17\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May trade surplus C$1.22 billion (April: C$1.20 billion)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7g00ppq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
