\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Morning: C$ Off Record Low, But Weak Trend Persists \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1998\par 15:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar is holding steady just below its all-time record low set Wednesday against the U.S. dollar in early trading Thursday, as the U.S. unit gathers momentum for a fresh assault on even higher levels. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.4880 at 9:45 a.m. EDT (1345 GMT), from C$1.4865 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) and C$1.4885 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that Canadian dollar selling interest appears to be mounting as the morning session advances, after the Canadian unit enjoyed a brief respite overnight in international markets. \par \par \uc2  After a record-setting day Wednesday when the Canadian dollar plunged through a 100-tick range and drew several rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its support from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. dollar's gains were temporarily stalled by a weaker overnight performance against the Japanese yen, and by uncertainty over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intentions on the interest rate front. \par \par \uc2  "People tried to get themselves a little bit long in Canada this morning in the off-chance that the Bank of Canada might move interest rates higher," said one trader at a major Canadian bank in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  But since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to nudge rates higher in its customary "window" just before 9:00 a.m. EDT (1300 GMT), the trader said the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected come under renewed pressure in the remainder of Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "It's going to be a bit of a 'bank hunt' from now on," he said. "The market's just going to see how high we can move the U.S. dollar to take on the bank." \par \par \uc2  Market participants said there is some support for the Canadian dollar at U.S. dollar levels between C$1.4900 and C$1.4925, but the U.S. unit's short-term target on technical factors is C$1.4945. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 9:45 a.m. EDT (1345 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Wednesday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.4880      1.4865    1.4885\par    CDN/DEM     1.2040      1.2051    1.2076\par    CDN/YEN     94.88       93.54     94.36\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-07-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1348GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7g061ah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
