\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar opens weaker, but off new low. \b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1998\par 15:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, July 15 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar hit another record low of C$1.4843 (US$0.6737) in early North American trade on Wednesday, after opening at C$1.4816 (US$0.6749), then the lowest intraday point. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been sliding to record lows every day with the previous all-time low just recorded overnight at C$1.4823 (US$0.6746). \par \par \uc2  "It's pretty bearish. The comment from Ottawa did not help yesterday. They are not showing any particular concern in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Canadian Prime Minister Jean Chretien told reporters on Tuesday that a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually helps exports and tourism. "It's not a question of being happy. It's a reality of life," he said. \par \par \uc2  And the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been quiet about the loonie's performance. No \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the bank to sell U.S. dollars for \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been detected in recent trade, with the slide coming in narrow movements. \par \par \uc2  "There's always speculation of an interest rate hike, but they've let it go this far," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  Canada's economic indicators weighed on the market this morning. \par \par \uc2  May manufacturing shipments fell 1.0 percent after a revised drop of 0.7 percent in April, while economists had forecast a 0.6-percent rise. May car sales came in lower than expected, rising 1.1 percent after a 5.9-percent rise in April. \par \par \uc2  In cross trading, the Canadian unit fell to 1.2126 marks from 1.2163 marks at the previous close here, but was flat at 94.47 yen after 94.46 yen. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has indicated that wider fluctuations of \par \par \uc2  monetary conditions are expected in Canada. It is watching \par \par \uc2  movements in the nation's short-term interest rates and the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's performance against other Group of 10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for \par \par \uc2  any signs of drastic easing in overall monetary conditions. \par \par \uc2  In theory, if Canada raised domestic interest rates, it \par \par \uc2  might be able to reverse the flow of capital to the U.S., at \par \par \uc2  least partly, and boost the value of the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  But analysts expect the bank of stay on hold for now. \par \par \uc2  External factors, such as concern over Asia and Russia, \par \par \uc2  affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a rate hike would not be warranted when \par \par \uc2  some economic indicators are showing signs of slowdown. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the Canadian unit came under heavy selling after \par \par \uc2  the nation's employment fell for the second consecutive month \par \par \uc2  in June, by 35,900 to 14.24 million after a drop of 7,300 in \par \par \uc2  May. Housing starts dropped 4.6 percent in June, the third \par \par \uc2  straight month of declines. \par \par \uc2  Consensus forecasts for key Canadian economic indicators \par \par \uc2  for the rest of the week (hit ECI/CI + F9 for a full list): \par \par \uc2     Thursday, JULY 16 \par \par \uc2     June CPI all items +1.1 percent (May: +1.1) \par \par \uc2     June CPI core rate +1.3 percent (May: +1.4) \par \par \uc2     Friday, JULY 17 \par \par \uc2  May trade surplus C$1.22 billion (April: C$1.20 billion) \par \par \uc2   (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107, \par \par \uc2  toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7f00y8q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
