\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar ends at new closing low of C$1.4890. \b0\par\par\uc2 986 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1998\par 22:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.4855/1.4940\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.4813\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US$ SUPPORT 1.4815  RESISTANCE 1.5035 HIGH 1.4823 LOW 1.4800\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.4816 HIGH 1.4895\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.4810\par PREV CLOSE  1.4810 LOW  1.4810\tab HIGH 1.4821 LOW 1.4797\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WEDNESDAY, JULY 15\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: NEUTRAL ACTIVITY: ACTIVE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada's dollar ended at record closing low of C$1.4890 (US$0.6716) against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. dollar. *CAD, which has been sliding constantly for past four months,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had hit a record trading low of C$1.4895 (US$0.6714) earlier in the afternoon\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow the pace of depreciation,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par starting at C$1.4870 (US$0.6725). *Weaker-than-expected data weighed on CAD,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par while the U.S. dollar stayed afloat on uncertainty over Japan's choice of its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par next PM after trimming overnight gains vs yen. *Canada May manufacturer\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shipments were down 1.0 percent from revised drop of 0.7 percent in April,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par while economists had forecast 0.6 percent rise. *Canada May car sales rose 1.1\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent, lower than forecast, after a 5.9 percent rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, July 15 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar on Wednesday ended at a record closing low of C$1.4890 (US$0.6716) against the U.S. dollar as signs of slower domestic economic growth weighed on the already weak local dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian unit, which has been sliding constantly for the past four months, had hit a record trading low of C$1.4895 (US$0.6714) earlier in the afternoon despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow the pace of depreciation. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  started at C$1.4870 (US$0.6725).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After opening at C$1.4816 (US$0.6749) on Wednesday, Canada's dollar came under downward pressure from another set of weaker-than-expected economic data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May manufacturing shipments fell 1.0 percent after a revised drop of 0.7 percent in April, while economists had forecast a 0.6-percent rise. May car sales came in lower than expected, rising 1.1 percent after a 5.9-percent rise in April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, the Canadian unit continued to slip to 1.2086 marks from 1.2163 marks at the previous close here, and was down slightly at 94.37 yen after 94.46 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's pretty bearish. The comment from Ottawa did not help yesterday. They\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are not showing any particular concern in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," one trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada's Prime Minister Jean Chretien told reporters on Tuesday that a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cheap \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  actually helps exports and tourism. "It's not a question of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par being happy. It's a reality of life," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the chart, the market has broken through the top of a two-week bull\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par channel for the U.S. dollar against Canada, signifying the acceleration of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par move, said Mark Roberts, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  technical analyst at I.D.E.A in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This should take us up to a larger channel, which has been in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for four months, and resistance for that is up at C$1.4950 (US$0.6689). I look\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for it to get up there for the next one to two days," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At that level, there might be a pullback or small consolidation before the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollar targets C$1.5000 (US$0.6667), a psychological barrier, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Interim resistance at 1.4855 (US$0.6732) on the way up to the current level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offers the U.S. dollar immediate support.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market always speculates for a key lending rate increase by the Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada as a means of defending the battered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but analysts are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sceptical about the effect of such action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Historical relationships suggest that higher interest rates have only\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limited impact," said Mark Chandler, senior economist at Goldman Sachs Canada.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "A 100-basis point increase in Canada-U.S. short term interest rate spreads\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par typically leads to less than a one-percent appreciation in the Canadian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Our best guess is that the bank will indeed hold rates constant through\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the end of the year," he wrote in a commentary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He argues that the depreciation of the loonie has provided an offset to a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decline in commodities prices, which would have otherwise been felt in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par employment. Commodities still account for nearly 40 percent of Canada's total\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has indicated that wider fluctuations of monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par conditions are expected in Canada. It is watching movements in the nation's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-term interest rates and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's performance against other Group of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for any signs of drastic easing in overall money conditions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In theory, if Canada raised domestic interest rates, it might be able to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reverse the flow of capital to the U.S., at least partly, and boost the value\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the Canadian dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But external factors, such as concern over Asia and Russia, affect the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and a rate hike would not be warranted when some economic indicators\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are showing signs of slowdown.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last week, the Canadian unit came under heavy selling pressure after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nation's employment fell for the second consecutive month in June, by 35,900 to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 14.24 million after a drop of 7,300 in May. Housing starts dropped 4.6 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in June, the third straight month of declines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Consensus forecasts for key Canadian economic indicators for the rest of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the week:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Thursday, JULY 16\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    June CPI all items +1.1 percent (May: +1.1)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    June CPI core rate +1.3 percent (May: +1.4)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Friday, JULY 17\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May trade surplus C$1.22 billion (April: C$1.20 billion)   (Masaru Sato,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7f00uic\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
