\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar breaks to record lows beyond C$1.48. \b0\par\par\uc2 623 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 1998\par 14:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 13 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar broke to new record lows on Monday in European trading after surpassing the psychological C$1.48 level earlier in Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prodded further along its recent weakening path by Friday's unemployment numbers, which revealed an increasingly fragile economy. \par \par \uc2  "Friday's figures were not looking too good and overall if you look at the Canadian economy you've got the problems with the weak commodity prices and shockwaves from the Asian situation," said Derek Shewring, senior dealer at Royal Bank of Canada. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to continue to suffer and we're looking for a test towards C$1.50." \par \par \uc2  Statistics Canada reported on Friday that the nation's unemployment rate held steady in June at 8.4 percent, unchanged from May. But employment fell by 35,900 to 14.24 million in June. It also fell by 7,300 in May. \par \par \uc2  Dealers at other Canadian banks in London said they also expected the Canadian dollar to head towards a test of C$1.50 by the end of the summer, but that a sharp drop could prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We're still targeting C$1.50, but if this thing shoots up quickly the Bank of Canada is going to have to come in to stem the tide," said a dealer at a Canadian bank in London. \par \par \uc2  At 1120 GMT the Canadian dollar was trading at C$1.4785/90 ($0.6761/64) after setting a new record low of C$1.4814 ($0.6749) compared with C$1.4793/98 ($0.6757/59). \par \par \uc2  However, they said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be enough to staunch the flow of money exiting Canadian investments because of low interest rates and a fragile economy. \par \par \uc2  They said the Canadian dollar will continue on its weakening trend as long as yields in Canada remain below those in the U.S. and economic data show economic growth may be slipping. \par \par \uc2  Canada's three-month T-bill was trading at a yield of 4.80/77 percent on Monday compared with U.S. three-month treasuries at 4.94 percent. \par \par \uc2  The softer economy and dollar are likely to test the Bank of Canada's resolve, which may have to make the choice of whether it prefers to see the dollar fall further and faster or economic growth injured if the bank raised in interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "With the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above C$1.48 there will be speculation that the Bank will hike, but I'm not sure the Bank of Canada can do too much given the state of the economy," Shewring said. \par \par \uc2  In other dollar bloc \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Aussie and Kiwi dollars hit two-week lows under pressure from renewed weakness in the yen. \par \par \uc2  Dollar bloc's Asian partners came under renewed selling pressure against the U.S. dollar as dollar/yen soared on losses to Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) in Sunday's election for the Upper House of Japan's parliament. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto resigned over the electoral defeats, which are as a major blow to the LDP party. \par \par \uc2  At 1135 GMT, the Australian dollar was at $0.6108/13, off a one-week low of $0.6029, but still down from $0.6142/52 in late European trading on Friday. The New Zealand dollar was at $0.5114/21, off a low of $0.5059, but still down from $0.5138/45 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  ((Paul Casciato, London newsroom +44 171 542 8968 fax +44 171 542 5293, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7d00v2t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
